#!/bin/bash
# golden-help — list the commands a golden laptop has and what they do.
cat <<'TXT'
Golden laptop commands

  Laptop and recipe
    golden-status            What the golden install did, and what is left to do by hand
    golden-status --watch    Follow an install or update while it runs
    sudo golden-update.sh    Update this laptop from the recipe on GitHub (main)
                             (full path: /opt/golden/ubuntu/firstboot/golden-update.sh)
    golden-projects          Clone the repositories listed in the golden settings

  deck: disposable media and browsing VM (KVM)
    deck                     Start it full screen. Close the window (or Power Off inside) to stop;
                             everything from the session is thrown away
                             (Ubuntu, dark; Firefox with DuckDuckGo and uBlock Origin; user deck / password deck)
                             Connects Proton VPN (Switzerland) with kill switch first, disconnects after; won't start
                             without it. deck --no-vpn skips the VPN
    deck-update              Install updates into its clean base (deck closed; about 2 minutes).
                             Also done by the weekly update (below)
    deck-create              Build it (the first login does this; about 15 minutes)
    deck-create --rebuild    Delete it and build it again
    In the VM window:        Ctrl+Alt releases mouse and keyboard; Shift+F11 leaves full screen

  Updates
    Automatic, weekly        Monday (or the first chance after) when on mains power and idle 10+ min:
                             Ubuntu packages, snaps, Flatpaks and deck. A notification says when it
                             starts and ends, and if a restart is needed. Log: /var/log/golden-weekly-update.log
    Run it now               sudo systemctl start golden-weekly-update   (still waits for idle and mains)

  VPN
    vpn-chain [COUNTRY]      Double VPN: Proton (default Estonia, kill switch on), then DCM through it
    vpn-chain off            DCM down, then Proton down; kill switch back as it was
    vpn-chain status         What is connected, and whether DCM really goes through Proton
    protonvpn connect --country CH / protonvpn disconnect / protonvpn status

  Power
    Lid closed on charger    Nothing happens (keeps running); on battery it suspends
    deck window open         The laptop does not dim, lock or suspend

  Handy system commands
    fwupdmgr get-updates     Firmware/BIOS updates waiting (apply: sudo fwupdmgr update)
    powerprofilesctl         Power mode: performance / balanced / power-saver
    ssh-copy-id <host>       Put this laptop's SSH key on a server in ~/.ssh/config
    virt-manager             Other virtual machines (KVM)
TXT
